\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2.4}{\ignorespaces Construction of depth cues for a 2D bar chart. First, the amount of depth is set by defining the opposite face of the standard 2D rectangular shape. Then the faces are connected and volume is filled in.\relax }}{15}{figure.caption.8}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2.5}{\ignorespaces Figure in Statistical Graphics: Design Principles and Practices. The viewing angle for this chart would have viewers overestimate the values of the bars\relax }}{17}{figure.caption.9}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2.6}{\ignorespaces Multiple charts of the volcano dataset (R Core Team 2024) rendered using the \texttt {rgl} package (Murdoch and Adler 2023) in R. Each chart has a different field-of-view parameter, with the amount of distortion increasing as the field-of-view (FOV) increases.\relax }}{19}{figure.caption.10}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2.7}{\ignorespaces Two examples of 3D bar charts found in publication (\emph {1978 Handbook of Agricultural Charts. Enlargements / {[}u.s. Department of Agriculture{]}} 1978). This left image is a stacked bar chart, using shadings to indicate sugarbeats and sugarcane. The image on the right\relax }}{21}{figure.caption.11}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2.11}{\ignorespaces Examples of color, size, and shape for scatterplots of the penguins dataset (Horst, Hill, and Gorman 2020).\relax }}{24}{figure.caption.16}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2.12}{\ignorespaces Heatmaps created with data from (XXX). The 2D heatmap represents the percentage of high school graduates using a gradient color scale, whereas the 3D heatmap uses height.\relax }}{25}{figure.caption.17}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2.13}{\ignorespaces Two figures representing the volcano dataset (R Core Team 2024) using different height scaling factors. Both figures use the same color scale, but there is no ``correct'' translation of color into the measurable height.\relax }}{25}{figure.caption.18}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2.14}{\ignorespaces Effect of color deficiencies on the inferno palette from Garnier et al. (2024).\relax }}{26}{figure.caption.19}%
